Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Meridian: Connect Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Copilot CLI,
 Gemini CLI, Qwen Code, Goose, Amp and Factory Droid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The same one-click Connect as Claude Code, Codex, Claude Desktop and
OpenCode, in Settings › AI and the first run, each the agent's own
user-level way:

- by its command: VS Code `code --add-mcp '{"name":"meridian",…}'` (the
  user profile's mcp.json; `code` from the app when it isn't on the PATH),
  GitHub Copilot CLI `copilot mcp add meridian -- …`, Gemini CLI and Qwen
  Code `<cli> mcp add -s user meridian <Meridian> -- --mcp-bridge`;
- by its config file, the way OpenCode is (other keys kept, the first old
  file kept as <file>.meridian-backup, links followed, a file that isn't
  plain JSON left alone with the snippet to add, idempotent): Cursor
  ~/.cursor/mcp.json and Windsurf ~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json
  ("mcpServers"), Amp ~/.config/amp/settings.json ("amp.mcpServers"),
  Factory Droid ~/.factory/mcp.json (a "stdio" server);
- Goose: an extension in config.yaml ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/goose, else
  ~/.config/goose), added without a YAML library only to the plain block
  style Goose writes; anything else is left alone with the snippet.

One generic JSON path covers OpenCode and the new files. Each file agent
has a test switch for its config folder (--meridian-cursor-config, …); in
a test without it the agent is never found. Found: on the login PATH, its
app, or its config folder. Settings lists the four as before plus any
other agent found, and names the rest; after Connect it says which app to
restart (or to start a new CLI session). The first run says "We found
<first agent>" and, after Yes, which apps to restart.

